cff-version: 1.2.0
title: VetPOC Constitution Corpus
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, please cite it and the Digital Judiciary programme
  papers it instantiates.
type: dataset
version: 2.4.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
authors:
  - family-names: Kadambi
    given-names: Arun
  - family-names: Kuppuswamy
    given-names: Venkat
    affiliation: >-
      D'Amore-McKim School of Business, Northeastern University
abstract: >-
  An open 6,000-case conformance corpus for governing software change in
  veterinary practice-management and point-of-care systems under a Digital
  Judiciary: a constitution of 98 provisions (18 absolute), a contest-gated
  admission rule, a distinguishing gate, a lexicographic ordering over
  conflicting precedents, and a store of binding decision records with an
  enforced lifecycle. Ground truth is computed from an executed trace rather
  than authored. Ships a reference adjudication engine, 26 conformance checks
  and a mutation matrix.
keywords:
  - compliance
  - precedent
  - policy-as-code
  - veterinary software
  - AI governance
  - conformance testing
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      When Retrieval Binds: Appraisal, Authenticity and Disposition in
      Automated Compliance Decisions
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Case-Base Formation for Precedential Constraint: Standing, Admission
      Rules, and the Reason Model
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
